💡 **SUGGESTION: error line fires before the resume-retry path is decided**

The new `console.error('❌ Pull Request creation failed — no PR exists for ...')` runs *before* `resumeDevelopmentAgent(...)` is consulted. When the resume path returns `true`, `action(params)` recurses and may well end with a successfully created PR — but the job log now permanently contains a `❌ ... no PR exists` error line for a leg that ultimately succeeded. That re-introduces a (much milder) form of log/Outcome mismatch: a future reader grepping for `❌` will find a failure that never was one.

Consider either moving the `console.error` after the `resumeDevelopmentAgent` check (so it only logs when the failure is final), or logging the resume attempt explicitly, e.g.:

```javascript
if (resumeDevelopmentAgent(params, ticketKey, _customParams, 'development_pr_creation', prResult.error)) {
    console.log('Resuming development agent to retry PR creation...');
    return action(params);
}
console.error('❌ Pull Request creation failed — no PR exists for ' + ticketKey + ':', prResult.error);
```

Not blocking — the thrown `prCreationFailure` guarantee (the actual gh-1197 contract) is unaffected.

